        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "5e9753e1-4008-57d9-8478-7358fbba24de",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Plants: Bulbophyllum, Bismarckia, Bismarckia nobilis\n- People: Otto von Bismarck, Jaap J. Vermeulen\n- Roles: botanist, chancellor\n- Concepts: Orchidaceae, flowering plants, Latin naming, palm susceptibility\n- Animals: Rhynchophorus cruentatus\n\nFacts:\n- Otto von Bismarck was the first chancellor of the German Empire.\n- Bismarckia is named after Otto von Bismarck.\n- The species epithet of Bismarckia nobilis comes from Latin for \"noble.\"\n- Jaap J. Vermeulen was born in 1955 and is a Dutch botanist.\n- Jaap J. Vermeulen specializes in the Orchidaceae genus Bulbophyllum.\n- Bulbophyllum is the largest genus in the orchid family Orchidaceae.\n- Bulbophyllum has more than 2,000 species.\n- Bulbophyllum is one of the largest genera of flowering plants and is exceeded only by Astragalus.\n- Rhynchophorus cruentatus mainly targets the Canary Island date palm.\n- Rhynchophorus cruentatus can also infest date palms, sabal palms, saw palmetto, Washingtonia, Pritchardia, royal palms, Latania, coconut palms, Caryota, and Bismarckia.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "4bb87360-c67f-5641-aff9-2ff4907cdbb6",
        "text": "Page: Bulbophyllum. Sentence: Bulbophyllum is the largest genus in the orchid family Orchidaceae.\nPage: Bulbophyllum. Sentence: With more than 2,000 species, it is also one of the largest genera of flowering plants, exceeded only by \"Astragalus\".\nPage: Bismarckia. Sentence: The genus is named for the first chancellor of the German Empire Otto von Bismarck and the epithet for its only species, Bismarckia nobilis, comes from Latin for 'noble'.\nPage: Jaap J. Vermeulen. Sentence: Jaap J. Vermeulen (born 1955) is a Dutch Botanist, specializing in the Orchidaceae Genus Bulbophyllum\nPage: Rhynchophorus cruentatus. Sentence: Its main target is the Canary Island date palm, but date palms (a different species than the Canary Island date palm), sabal palms (the palmetto weevil's traditional target), saw palmetto (the palmetto weevil's traditional alternative target), \"Washingtonia\", \"Pritchardia\", royal palms, \"Latania\", coconut palms, \"Caryota\", and \"Bismarckia\" are also susceptible.",
        "type": "DocumentChunk"
      },
